WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.320
kanashimi sasou midnight

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.320
Such a sad midnight,

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:09.260
koboreru ai o choudai

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:09.260
overflowing with love.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.830
kiiroi ringo o kajitteru

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.770
Gnawing at a yellow apple,

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.790
kimi wa hitoshirezu otona ni naru

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.790
you secretly become an adult.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.230
tameiki iro shite mayoikomu

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.230
You sigh, having lost your way

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:31.000
ai o sagashite ikiteru

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:31.000
living in a search for love.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:35.280
suki yo tabun ne dakedo

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:35.280
Maybe I love you, but—

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.720
akai tsuki ga miteru

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.720
the red moon is watching,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:45.310
konna ni mo chikaku ni iru no ni

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:45.310
it waits nearby.

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:49.770
kanashimi sasou midnight

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:49.770
Such a sad midnight.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.840
I can say love

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.570
koboreru ai o choudai

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.570
It overflows with love.

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:53.570
will you love me?

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:57.180
tomadoi no hitomi no oku

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:57.180
Lost within your eyes,

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:00.130
kokyuu o tomete

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:00.130
I stop breathing.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.690
kimi no ai o katachi ni

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.690
The shape of your love,

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:08.340
mayonaka no taiyou

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:08.340
is like the midnight sun.

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:29.370
This place is practically a maze...

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.840
I should've brought NB with me.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:46.830
Baptism

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:48.420
Next.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.760
Hahm Clay, coming in.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.340
Next!

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.330
Nick Idoth, coming in.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:20.490
Change it! Please!

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:21.990
Change what?

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.590
Seina-kun's training post!

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:26.460
Oh, so that's what this is about?

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:29.830
Assigning him there, of all places...!

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:33.070
Now, now. There's no need to describe it like that.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:36.140
It's a wonderful subdivision of the GP.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.610
T-that's not what I meant...

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.010
The GP was created as a means for dealing with crime.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.580
More importantly, though, is the prevention of crime before it can occur.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.320
Having pirates raid transport ships is a real problem,

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.120
even if we do catch them afterward.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:53.920
In which case, it's fairly obvious where he would be best suited.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:55.960
Next!

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.950
Seina Yamada, coming in!

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:17.000
Student Number S25-5963. Seina Yamada.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:21.480
GP Delivery Department, Business Affairs Section.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:25.250
You are hereby assigned to train as a member of the Decoy Transport Unit.

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:29.230
D-decoy...?

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:31.130
It means just what it says.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.630
An anti-pirate decoy unit.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:38.300
It's perfect for you, don't you think?

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.670
You knew, didn't you?

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:42.310
No, I hadn't the slightest...

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:45.640
Erma. Thanks for taking care of the formalities.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:51.780
Well, I suppose it probably is the perfect post for Seina.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.120
Make sure you attract plenty of pirates, okay?

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.520
R-right...

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.320
Most people think of hotshot detectives

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:06.400
or highly-specialized missions when they think of the GP,

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.700
but most of the funds used to maintain the GP come from its delivery services.

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:15.470
Every planet out there views it as their main artery for trade and delivery.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:17.670
You could even call it their lifeline.

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:21.540
The fate of the GP depends on your actions as a decoy!

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:26.050
In other words, our very livelihood rests in your hands, Seina.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.350
Yes...

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.560
Sorry about this afternoon...

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:40.260
No, that's OK. You're right to be worried.

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:44.370
You are in Seina-kun's debt.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:45.470
So if you want to do something for him,

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.740
this is your chance for you two to be alone.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:51.110
Airi-sama! I'm not...

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:54.110
Seina-kun! Good luck with your new post!

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:55.700
R-right!

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.240
Bye!

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.930
Seina-chan...

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:12.400
You run away if you run into any pirates.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.470
A good decoy is one that can escape without getting hurt.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:18.460
Okay?

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:22.240
Yes!

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:39.320
I have to become a good decoy!

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:40.960
OK! Here I go!

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.260
But... which way?

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:48.060
Excuse me!

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:51.660
I'm looking for where they do decoy stuff for the Delivery Department...

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.970
Oh!

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.960
Mitoto-san?!

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.780
So you want to go to the Delivery Department?

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:07.020
Right, I need to get to my decoy unit...

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:09.220
Can we clean on the way there?

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.980
Sure...

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:19.930
Sorry for transferring you all the way here, Kiriko-kun.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:25.870
Oh no, I owe you so much that I simply couldn't turn down your offer.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:29.570
But you certainly are an odd one.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:35.140
You could easily be the information officer on any flagship of your choice,

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:37.750
so how come you're working as an academy instructor?

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:42.080
I'm simply obeying orders; I can't make such decisions on my own.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.920
You're more than welcome to return to the military if you ever feel so inclined.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.420
Thank you.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:49.190
But...

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:52.500
This is exciting enough for me!

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:55.160
Is it now?

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:59.530
Large pirate craft detected! Course bearing 070!

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.100
Distance 1050!

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:03.010
It appears they're aware of our presence!

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:04.770
They're approaching our position!

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:07.580
Accelerate to maximum velocity! Draw back!

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:10.010
Our mission takes maximum priority right now!

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:12.180
How can they know both our course and present location

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:15.120
if our ship is cloaked with a Storming Block?

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:16.450
Dumb luck?

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:20.120
Captain! Unauthorized personnel discovered in Corridor A!

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.110
Find out who they are, immediately!

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:25.190
I've identified them!

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:27.360
It looks like one of them is Mitoto Kuramitsu-sama,

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:28.970
and the other one is...

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:32.330
S-Seina-chan...?

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:38.610
All clean! Thank you so much, Seina-chan!

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:39.980
My pleasure!

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.540
So, about the Delivery Department...

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:45.650
This way! Oh, it's this way?

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:51.350
We've successfully led them into Dining Hall number 2!

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.390
Excellent! Now seal them in!

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:55.420
Do not let them get out of sight!

00:07:55.420 --> 00:08:00.860
I'm not sure how they got in, but it's a good thing we had pudding ready.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:04.200
I'm so sorry that one of my students snuck on board...

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:08.400
No, it's an honor to have the famous Seina Yamada-kun aboard my ship.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:11.470
I wouldn't have believed it without seeing it for myself,

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:14.670
but it appears he's as gifted as the rumors make him out to be.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:19.610
Though it would be best if he remains docile, if at all possible.

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:23.520
A new emergency!

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:26.260
Warp signature detected at U-152!

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:29.930
The pirate ship from earlier is exiting a jump!

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:33.730
That's crazy! They know that this is a warship!

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:43.330
T-that ship...!

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:55.990
There's no mistake!

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:57.650
It's the Daidalos!

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:00.860
The Daidalos...

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:02.590
Tarant Shank...

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:12.130
It had to be him, of all people!

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:14.640
Captain!

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:16.770
Use gravity charges to keep them at bay!

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:19.010
Calculate a point where our ship won't be affected

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:20.580
and then perform a random jump!

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.770
We must escape at all costs!

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.620
Crafty...

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:36.730
The enemy craft's course and speed remain unchanged!

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:39.320
We're now within tractor beam range!

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:44.760
Seina-chan...!

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:50.800
W-what the...?! Pudding! Pudding!

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:22.340
Blocks 3 and 7 have been overrun!

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:25.070
A fire has broken out in Block 5!

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:26.580
What about Mitoto-sama and Seina-kun?!

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:28.540
They're gone...

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:29.950
Wait.

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:32.920
They're moving from Corridor B to Block 2!

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:36.190
It'll take at least 450 seconds until a security dispatch can reach them!

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:37.390
Damn it...

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:39.650
We should've detained them when we had the chance!

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:44.260
Captain. There's only one way we can stand up to the Daidalos...

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:51.070
Please make sure nothing happens to Seina-kun...

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:53.270
Ensure the safety of the main engine!

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:55.370
The instant Mitoto-sama and Seina-kun arrive

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:58.270
we'll attach a fixed hook to the enemy vessel and get out of here!

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:48.760
What's the status of Mitoto-sama and Seina-kun?!

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:51.790
We still can't contact them and we can't predict their movement patterns!

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:54.630
No matter how much analysis we do, they do something completely different!

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:00.170
All done cleaning this area!

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:01.470
U-um...

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:04.010
Mitoto-san, about the Delivery Department...

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:06.530
Why don't we ask him?

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.510
Excuse me...

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:12.820
Sorry to bother you with a silly question, but...

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:14.250
Mitoto-san!

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:23.720
Go! Don't stop until the ship's ours!

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:32.360
W-who's there?!

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:44.380
All I did was ask for directions... He must be in a bad mood...

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:47.820
This isn't the time for that!

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:09.040
And here I was thinkin' this was some old and worthless warship...

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:10.370
A hunt, eh?

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:12.640
Tarant-sama isn't very considerate...

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:17.740
Putting me in charge of the ship while he goes and has all the fun...

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:22.320
Energy anomaly detected inside the enemy ship...?

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.420
Oh, shit!

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:26.410
Damn them! I have to contact Tarant-sama immediately!

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:07.690
Hurry! This way!

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:13.930
What? A Guardian...?!

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:33.380
Come on! Hurry!

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:43.600
Sorry it took so long to rescue you, Mitoto-sama!

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:45.570
No, that's okay!

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:50.940
But this is the first time pirates have ever attacked a GP spaceport...

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:54.510
Mitoto-sama! We're inside a warship!

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:56.850
Oh my! I did it again!

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:59.950
I'm so sorry, Seina-chan. He says we're on the wrong ship...

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:02.040
I-I heard...

00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:06.690
It's Tarant Shank!

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:10.090
The Tarant...?

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:22.030
Yamada-kun! Quickly!

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:42.590
I never expected us to meet in a place like this...

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.080
Seina Yamada.

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:53.100
My incompetent old man was caught because of a single GP ship...

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:56.800
Do you have any idea how much shame that brought upon me?!

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:03.150
This will make the perfect coffin for you.

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:07.250
Where should I give you your new hole?

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:08.480
Here?

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:11.750
Or... Here?

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:16.280
I'll enjoy watching you die slowly...

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:24.370
Who's there?!

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:33.500
Damn, optical camouflage...

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:39.940
K-Kiriko-san...!

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:06.370
Damn you...!

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:23.290
How dare you...

00:17:39.940 --> 00:17:43.610
No matter where you run away to...

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:48.350
...I will hunt you down and kill you.

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:54.960
We don't have any time!

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:56.420
Let's get out of here!

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:34.930
I see.

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.200
So you came face to face with him just like that?

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:48.540
It was probably bound to happen at some point anyway...

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:51.750
Even though Kiriko-san saved me...

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:55.180
Even though I couldn't do anything...

00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:57.780
I was so afraid of her...!

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:02.760
This is so humiliating!

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:06.190
I want to be strong!

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:27.520
It's all right.

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:29.850
I'll help you.

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:41.830
This is the decoy ship, Kamidake?

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:43.930
Pretty sweet looking, if you ask me...

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:48.400
Well, ideally, a decoy should look impressive,

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:52.070
so although it's kind of small it'll definitely get the job done.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:56.650
But what kind of captain would they choose for a ship like this?

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:59.950
Probably some pathetic loser who can't get any real assignments!

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:04.350
Or maybe some old pervert who was reprimanded for sexual harassment!

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:11.190
And to think that we'll have to call him our captain...

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:12.890
Oh, here comes the captain!

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:14.330
Salute!

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:17.460
Allow us to take your baggage, Captain!

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:22.600
Captain?

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:23.700
Huh?

00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:32.270
Dangerous turn of events, eh?

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:41.060
Amane-sensei...

00:20:41.060 --> 00:20:44.030
I'm not your teacher anymore... Captain.

00:20:44.030 --> 00:20:48.400
But I don't blame you. Your status did suddenly change, after all...

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:51.370
As did mine... And hers...

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:08.910
I'm sorry...

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:18.490
Ahem.

00:21:18.490 --> 00:21:20.650
Oh, right...

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:28.770
Those are some fine secretaries you got there, boss.

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:32.330
Yessiree, there's gonna be plenty of action aboard this ship...

00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:21.740
uchuu de saitei saiaku

00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:21.740
You're the worst, most hopeless,

00:22:21.780 --> 00:22:26.860
un warui Unlucky Boy

00:22:21.780 --> 00:22:26.860
most unlucky boy in space.

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:34.070
anna koto shite te mo

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:34.070
No matter what you do,

00:22:35.090 --> 00:22:36.800
konna koto shite te mo

00:22:35.090 --> 00:22:36.800
no matter what you do,

00:22:37.070 --> 00:22:41.590
otozureru jiko tensai sugoi wana

00:22:37.070 --> 00:22:41.590
you can't escape the accidents, disasters and traps

00:22:41.590 --> 00:22:43.880
anata wa nigerarenai

00:22:41.590 --> 00:22:43.880
that come your way.

00:22:45.680 --> 00:22:47.450
keikai shite te mo

00:22:45.680 --> 00:22:47.450
Even if your really careful...

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:50.160
ikinari shichatte mo

00:22:48.430 --> 00:22:50.160
And even if you're not...

00:22:50.420 --> 00:22:56.390
saitei saiaku dame dame no

00:22:50.420 --> 00:22:56.390
You're the worst and most hopeless...

00:22:56.390 --> 00:23:00.860
anata wa doshiyou mo nai

00:22:56.390 --> 00:23:00.860
You're a lost cause.

00:23:05.710 --> 00:23:10.810
anata ga saitei saiaku

00:23:05.710 --> 00:23:10.810
You're the worst and most hopeless...

00:23:11.260 --> 00:23:15.430
anata wa Unlucky Boy

00:23:11.260 --> 00:23:15.430
You're an unlucky boy.

00:23:15.430 --> 00:23:20.510
dakedo anata shika mienai

00:23:15.430 --> 00:23:20.510
But all I can see is you,

00:23:20.690 --> 00:23:26.030
sonna anata shika mienai

00:23:20.690 --> 00:23:26.030
just the way you are.

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:33.940
My training as captain of the decoy transport ship for

00:23:33.940 --> 00:23:36.940
the Delivery Department has begun.

00:23:36.940 --> 00:23:38.980
The GP really is great!

00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:41.620
We get paid even while we're training!

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:43.620
Next time on Tenchi Muyo GXP!

00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:45.590
First Paycheck and Presents
